  "title": "Novo Alternatives for Small Business Banking in 2026",
  "h1": "Novo Alternatives for Small Business Banking in 2026",
  "metaDescription": "Novo alternatives compared: Mercury, Relay, Bluevine, Lili, Wise Business and Chase, with monthly fees, savings rates and deposit insurance limits.",
  "published": "2026-11-21",
  "updated": "2026-11-21",
  "intro": "Mercury, Relay, Bluevine, Lili, Wise Business and Chase Business Complete Banking are six Novo alternatives for small business banking. The right one depends on whether a business wants interest on checking balances, multiple checking accounts, in-branch service, multi-currency transfers or built-in lending. The table lists each provider's published fees, and the sections below work out plan costs and interest over a full year.\n\n[Novo](https://www.novo.co/) is a financial technology (fintech) company. It is not a bank. Banking services come from Middlesex Federal Savings, F.A., Member Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC), and Novo lists FDIC insurance up to $5,000,000 per depositor through Middlesex and other banks in its sweep network.\n\nNovo Business Checking has no monthly service fee, no fee to open, no minimum balance and free standard Automated Clearing House (ACH) transfers. The checking account does not earn interest. Novo Savings, opened alongside checking, pays 2% annual percentage yield (APY) once the balance is $50,000 or more, and Novo reimburses third-party automated teller machine (ATM) fees up to $7 at the end of each month.\n\nFor related shortlists, see the [best business bank accounts roundup](/roundup/best-business-bank-accounts/), the [Mercury alternatives](/alternatives/mercury/) guide and the [best business credit cards roundup](/roundup/best-business-credit-cards/). The [best accounting software for freelancers roundup](/roundup/best-accounting-software-for-freelancers/) covers bookkeeping tools, and the [comparison hub](/compare/) holds wider software and finance breakdowns.",
